---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = 'How to Play Poople: Rules, Tips & Word Ladder Strategies';
const pageDescription = 'Master Poople with our complete guide: basic rules, step-by-step word ladder strategies, common traps to avoid, and BFS shortest path techniques.';

const schemas = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'How to Play Poople: Official Rules & Strategies',
    description: 'A comprehensive tutorial on solving the daily Poople word ladder game.',
    author: {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'Poople Answer Today',
      url: 'https://poopleanswertoday.com',
    },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://poopleanswertoday.com' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'How to Play', item: 'https://poopleanswertoday.com/how-to-play' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} schema={schemas}>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-8 sm:py-12 space-y-8">
    <div class="space-y-3 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-ink tracking-tight">
        How to Play <span class="text-brand">Poople</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base text-ink-muted">
        Rules, advanced ladder strategies, and tips to solve the daily puzzle in minimum steps.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Guide Content -->
    <article class="bg-white border-2 border-paper-border rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-warm-md space-y-8 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-ink">
      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-ink flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-paper-border pb-2">
          <span>🎯</span> The Core Objective
        </h2>
        <p>
          Poople is a daily <strong>word ladder</strong> game invented by Lewis Carroll in 1877. In Poople, your goal is to transform a given <strong>4-letter starting word</strong> into the goal word <strong class="text-brand">POOP</strong> in the minimum possible number of moves.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Rules -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-ink flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-paper-border pb-2">
          <span>📜</span> The Official Rules
        </h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-ink-muted">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">One Letter at a Time:</strong> Each transition must change exactly <strong>one letter</strong> from the previous word.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Valid English Words:</strong> Every transitional step must be a recognized 4-letter English word in the game's dictionary.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">No Length Change:</strong> Words must always remain exactly 4 letters long throughout the ladder.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Shortest Path Bonus:</strong> Your score depends on matching or getting close to the optimal shortest path (par).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Visual Example -->
      <section class="space-y-3 bg-paper-dark p-5 rounded-xl border border-paper-border">
        <h3 class="text-base font-black text-ink">Example Walkthrough (TEES → POOP)</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-ink-muted">
          Here is how <code class="font-bold">TEES</code> reaches <code class="font-bold">POOP</code> in 5 steps:
        </p>
        <div class="font-mono-tile text-sm font-bold text-brand-dark space-y-1">
          <p>1. TEES → <strong>P</strong>EES (Change 1st letter: T → P)</p>
          <p>2. PEES → PEE<strong>P</strong> (Change 4th letter: S → P)</p>
          <p>3. PEEP → P<strong>R</strong>EP (Change 2nd letter: E → R)</p>
          <p>4. PREP → PR<strong>O</strong>P (Change 3rd letter: E → O)</p>
          <p>5. PROP → P<strong>O</strong>OP (Change 2nd letter: R → O) 🏁</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Tips & Strategies -->
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-ink flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-paper-border pb-2">
          <span>🧠</span> Pro Tips & Winning Strategies
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-ink-muted">
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm sm:text-base">1. Work Backwards from "POOP"</h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
              Keep the immediate neighbors of <code>POOP</code> in mind: <code>PLOP</code>, <code>PROP</code>, <code>POLE</code>, <code>POLL</code>, <code>POLO</code>, <code>POOL</code>, <code>POOR</code>, <code>POPE</code>, <code>PORK</code>, <code>PORT</code>, <code>POST</code>, <code>POSH</code>. Your intermediate target is usually one of these gateway words.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm sm:text-base">2. Watch Out for First-Move Traps</h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
              Many neighbor words seem intuitive but actually branch into dead ends or add extra steps. Check our <a href="/" class="text-brand font-bold underline">daily hints</a> to see which branch is truly optimal.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm sm:text-base">3. Use the Unlimited Mode to Practice</h4>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm">
              The more 4-letter vocabulary patterns you recognize, the faster you will spot shortcuts. Train daily on our <a href="/unlimited" class="text-brand font-bold underline">Poople Unlimited</a> tool.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
